iology for cardiac failure.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b1-ijwh-5-001">1</xref></p></list-item><list-item><p>Absence of known heart disease prior to the last month of pregnancy.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b1-ijwh-5-001">1</xref></p></list-item><list-item><p>Left ventricular systolic dysfunction demonstrated by classic echocardiographic criteria such as depressed shortening fraction or ejection fraction.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b2-ijwh-5-001">2</xref></p></list-item></list></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-ijwh-5-001"><p><bold>Abbreviation:</bold> PPCM, peripartum cardiomyopathy.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-ijwh-5-001" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Geographic incidence of PPCM</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Country/area</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Years studied</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Incidence</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ethnicity of study cohort</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Incidence by ethnicity</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Author</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Japan</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2007&#x02013;2008</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:20,000</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Japanese 100%<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn3-ijwh-5-001">a</xref></td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Japanese (1:20,000)</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Kamiya et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b9-ijwh-5-001">9</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">United States</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1995&#x02013;2004</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:2066</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">White 41%, Hispanic 27%</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijwh-5-001">b</xref> (1:664)<break/>Filipino (1:978)<break/>White (1:2450)<break/>Hispanic (1:6729)</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Gunderson et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b7-ijwh-5-001">7</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">United States</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1990&#x02013;2002</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:3189</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">White 79%, AA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijwh-5-001">b</xref> 16%<break/>Other 5%</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not stated</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mielniczuk et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b5-ijwh-5-001">5</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">United States</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1996&#x02013;2005</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:4025</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijwh-5-001">b</xref> 28%, White 27%, Hispanic 20%, Asian 17%, Other 8%</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijwh-5-001">b</xref> (1:1421)<break/>Asians (1:2675)<break/>Whites (1:4075)<break/>Hispanic (1:9861)</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Brar et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b6-ijwh-5-001">6</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">United States Augusta, GA</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2003&#x02013;2008</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:540</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijwh-5-001">b</xref> 93%<break/>Other 7%</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijwh-5-001">b</xref> (1:294)<break/>Other (1:4167)</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Gentry et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b22-ijwh-5-001">22</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">South Africa</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1986&#x02013;1989</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:1000</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0201c;Black African&#x0201d; 99%<break/>Asian 1%</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not stated</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Desai et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b11-ijwh-5-001">11</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sudan</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1975&#x02013;1979</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:662</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not stated</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not stated</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Suliman<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b48-ijwh-5-001">48</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Haiti</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2000&#x02013;2005</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:300</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn5-ijwh-5-001">c</xref></td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not stated</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fett et al<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b10-ijwh-5-001">10</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Nigeria</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2003&#x02013;2005</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1:100</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Hausa and Fulani ethnic groups 85%</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not stated</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Isezuo and Abubakar<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b49-ijwh-5-001">49</xref></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn2-ijwh-5-001"><p><bold>Notes:</bold></p></fn><fn id="tfn3-ijwh-5-001"><label>a</label><p>Kamiya CA, personal communication, April 22, 2012;</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ijwh-5-001"><label>b</label><p>non-Hispanic AA;</p></fn><fn id="tfn5-ijwh-5-001"><label>c</label><p>authors report study population consisted of &#x0201c;an ethnic population overwhelmingly descended from West African slaves.&#x0201d;<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b10-ijwh-5-001">10</xref></p></fn><fn id="tfn6-ijwh-5-001"><p><bold>Abbreviations:</bold> PPCM, peripartum cardiomyopathy; AA, African American.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>